"""XAL5030-472MEC - 4.7 uH 20 % shielded power inductor, Coilcraft XAL5030 (5.28 x 5.48 x 3.1 mm). Bare part.

Datasheet: Coilcraft XAL50xx series, Document 908 (908-1 revised 06/23/23; the drawing and the
L vs Current plots from 908-2/-4 revised 07/15/13, whose XAL5030-472 row is the same), the URL in
pcb.toml. Role: the series choke of the fan motor behind the STSPIN958 at 400 kHz (next-revision
proposal, Fan): 4.7-10 uH, at most a 20 % inductance drop at the REF current limit (up to 4.31 A),
about 5 x 5 mm.

Electrical (Doc 908-1 table, XAL5030-472ME_ row; notes 2-7):
- L 4.7 uH +-20 % at 1 MHz, 0.1 Vrms, 0 Adc (note 2).
- DCR 36.00 mOhm typ, 40.00 mOhm max (note 3). SRF 23 MHz typ.
- Isat 6.7 A: the DC current at 25 C that lowers the inductance by 30 % typ (note 5); the table
  gives no 10 % or 20 % columns.
- Irms 4.3 A (20 C rise) and 5.9 A (40 C rise) from 25 C ambient (note 6).
- Ambient -40 to +125 C with the 40 C-rise Irms; operating voltage 0-60 V, above the 17.4 V 4S pack;
  terminations tin-silver over copper; mass 0.44-0.51 g (Doc 908-1).

20 % drop: the Doc 908-2 L vs Current plot of the 4.7 uH part, read point by point, keeps 97.7 /
95.0 / 91.5 / 87.2 / 82.2 / 76.6 % of its 5.0 uH zero-current value at 1 / 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 / 6 A and
falls 30 % at about 7.0 A. Coilcraft's saturation form fitted to it (flux = L Is tanh((I/Is)^a)^(1/a),
Is 12.7 A, a 0.87) falls 20 % at 5.32 A; with its current axis compressed so the 30 % drop lands
on the table's 6.7 A, 5.05 A. `isat_20` is 5.0 A.

Dimensions (Doc 908-4): 5.28 +-0.2 x 5.48 +-0.2 mm, 3.1 mm max height (XAL5030); bottom terminals
1.0 +-0.05 mm wide, 2.31 +-0.25 mm apart, A 4.18 +-0.2 mm long for the -472. Recommended land
pattern: 1.18 mm wide pads at 3.31 mm centre pitch, B 4.25 mm long for the -472; the footprint's
4.70 mm pads (the XGL5030's land, on which the board was routed) reach 0.26 mm past each end of
the terminals. The bar on the top marks the start (short) lead.

AC (core) loss (Coilcraft's power-inductor loss tool for this part, as recorded in
github.com/QY7/Power_toys, power_toys/data/coilcraft_loss_for_training/XAL5030-472.txt):
99.5 mW x dIpp^1.635 at 0.408 MHz, independent of the DC current and nearly linear in f; part
temperature rise 31.9 K/W (LossRth, coilcraft_model/XAL5030-472.txt). research
calculations/fan/fan_choke_check.py.

The `current` property is the lower of the 40 C-rise Irms and the 30 %-drop Isat, as for the
other inductor packages in this registry.
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Current", "Inductance", "Resistance")
load("@stdlib/utils.zen", "format_value")

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)

# Doc 908-1, XAL5030-472ME_ row.
inductance = Inductance("4.7uH 20%")
isat = Current("6.7A")  # 30 % drop, 25 C (note 5)
isat_20 = Current("5.0A")  # 20 % drop: Doc 908-2 plot, scaled to the 6.7 A Isat (docstring)
irms = Current("5.9A")  # 40 C rise; 4.3 A at 20 C rise
current = Current("5.9A")
dcr = Resistance("40mOhm")  # max; 36.00 mOhm typ

Component(
    name="XAL5030-472",
    prefix="L",
    symbol=Symbol(library="XAL5030-472.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("L_Coilcraft_XAL5030-XXX.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="XAL5030-472MEC", manufacturer="Coilcraft"),
    pins={"1": P1, "2": P2},
    properties={
        "value": format_value(inductance, current),
        "inductance": inductance,
        "current": current,
        "isat": isat,
        "isat_20": isat_20,
        "irms": irms,
        "dcr": dcr,
    },
    type="inductor",
)
